WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是詹娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专为你们录制了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能讲出的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office, ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.480
Season four.
第四季。

9
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.920
Season four.
第四季。

10
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.260
Holy guacamole.
我的天哪。

11
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.720
It's Fun Run.
这是慈善长跑。

12
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.200
It's Fun Run part one.
这是慈善长跑上集。

13
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.220
That's right.
没错。

14
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.420
Because Fun Run was an hour-long episode.
因为慈善长跑是一集长达一小时的剧集。

15
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.380
So once again, we're going to break it down into two parts.
所以我们再次将其分为上下两部分。

16
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.020
Today is Fun Run part one.
今天是慈善长跑上集。

17
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.540
Written by Greg Daniels.
由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧。

18
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.720
Directed by Greg Daniels.
由格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导。

19
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.660
So much happens in Fun Run.
慈善长跑里发生了太多事。

20
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.360
It needs to be two episodes.
它必须分成两集。

21
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.560
It really does.
确实如此。

22
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.940
Oh, for sure.
哦，绝对的。

23
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:54.880
For sure.
绝对的。

24
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.160
Here is a summary of just part one.
以下仅为上集的剧情梗概。

25
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.300
Yeah, let's hear it.
好的，让我们听听吧。

26
00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:58.960
Yeah, let's hear it.
好的，让我们听听吧。

27
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.600
Okay, Michael accidentally hits Meredith with his car and breaks her pelvis.
好吧，迈克尔开车不小心撞了梅雷迪思，撞碎了她的骨盆。

28
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.160
There's so much there already.
光是这些就已经够丰富的了。

29
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:08.600
Already.
已经够丰富的了。

30
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:15.740
He gets the whole gang to visit her in the hospital and later discovers she may also have rabies.
他叫上所有人去医院看望她，后来发现她可能还得了狂犬病。

31
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:23.000
Angela asks Dwight to give medicine to her cat, Sprinkles, while she visits Meredith in the hospital.
安吉拉请德怀特在她去医院看望梅雷迪思期间，给她的猫雪碧喂药。

32
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.360
But when Dwight returns, he announces that Sprinkles is dead and he puts Sprinkles in the freezer.
但德怀特回来时宣布雪碧死了，并把雪碧放进了冰柜里。

33
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.620
In the freezer!
放进冰柜里！

34
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.840
Also, your television was on.
另外，你的电视机开着。

35
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.920
Yeah, my television was on and Sprinkles is in the freezer.
对，我的电视机开着，而雪碧在冰柜里。

36
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.480
Meanwhile, everyone wants to know if Jim and Pam are dating.
与此同时，每个人都想知道吉姆和帕姆是否在交往。

37
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.720
They insist they're not.
他们坚称没有。

38
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.020
They say they're just friends.
他们说他们只是朋友。

39
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.280
But Kevin is not convinced.
但凯文并不相信。

40
00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.320
Kevin really has a bee in his bonnet about it.
凯文对这件事真的是耿耿于怀。

41
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.320
Yeah.
对。

42
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.420
Why does Kevin care so much?
凯文为什么这么关心？

43
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

44
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.420
He's obsessed.
他着魔了。

45
00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:06.520
Because this episode begins so dramatically, we felt like we needed to speak with the woman at the center of this episode.
因为这一集的开头太戏剧化了，我们觉得有必要和这一集核心的那位女性聊聊。

46
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:07.900
Absolutely.
绝对的。

47
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.540
We need to talk to Kate Flannery about getting hit by that car.
我们得跟凯特·弗兰纳里聊聊被车撞的事。

48
00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:13.580
Yes.
是的。

49
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.720
So, guys, Kate chatted with us.
所以，伙计们，凯特跟我们聊了聊。

50
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.380
Sam, will you play the interview?
萨姆，能放一下这段采访吗？

51
00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.410
Flannery is here today, you guys, with her tiny teacup.
大家看，弗兰纳里今天带着她的小茶杯来了。

52
00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.330
Hi, Kate.
嗨，凯特。

53
00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.110
How are you?
你好吗？

54
00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:29.650
I'm great.
我很好。

55
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.430
How are you guys doing?
你们最近怎么样？

56
00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.570
It's so nice to see you.
很高兴见到你们。

57
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:31.830
Wait.
等等。

58
00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.670
We have to get a picture of you with that teacup.
我们得拍张你拿着那个茶杯的照片。

59
00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:34.950
Cody, will you take a picture?
科迪，能帮拍张照吗？

60
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.230
It's not tiny.
它可不小。

61
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.970
It's a regular-sized teacup.
这是一个正常大小的茶杯。

62
00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.090
What's tiny about that?
那杯子哪里小了？

63
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:40.950
I don't believe you.
我才不信呢。

64
00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:41.610
It looks tiny.
看起来很小啊。

65
00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.450
It's regular.
是正常大小的。

66
00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.150
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

67
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.530
And you have a little cup and saucer.
而且你还有一个小茶杯和茶托。

68
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:47.750
I do.
没错。

69
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Guys, Kate Flannery is one of the classiest gals.
伙计们，凯特·弗兰纳里绝对是最有品味的姑娘之一。

70
00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.390
Her home is spectacular.
她的家简直绝了。

71
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.890
It is decorated like it's out of Architectural DigeSt.
那装修得就像从《建筑文摘》里搬出来的一样。

72
00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.310
It is – every little thing is amazing.
确实——每个小细节都惊艳无比。

73
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:06.610
And I am not surprised at all that you look so put together and you're having your tea in a proper cup and saucer.
你把自己收拾得这么精致，用精致的茶杯和茶托喝茶，我一点也不觉得奇怪。

74
00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:07.190
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

75
00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:07.450
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

76
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.470
But now I got to turn my phone off because someone's calling me.
不过我现在得把手机关了，因为有人在给我打电话。

77
00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:10.810
She's getting an important phone call.
她正接一个重要电话呢。

78
00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:11.510
Sorry.
抱歉。

79
00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.150
Take it on air.
直接在节目里接吧。

80
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:12.710
Take it on air.
直接在节目里接。

81
00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.330
Who is it?
是谁呀？

82
00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.170
Let's talk to them.
我们跟他们聊聊。

83
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.650
I can't get locked in a timeshare just for you for the bit.
我可不能为了节目效果，只为你们就被套牢去买分时度假房。

84
00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:21.370
I'm sorry, you guys.
不好意思，伙计们。

85
00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:21.830
I can't.
我不能接。

86
00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.570
It's so good to see you.
很高兴见到你们。

87
00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:24.530
You don't understand.
你们不明白。

88
00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.970
We spent every day together for nine years.
我们曾经连续九年天天黏在一起。

89
00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:28.810
I know.
我知道。

90
00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.110
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

91
00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.870
I know.
我知道。

92
00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.790
It was so much like a real office job in that respect.
从这方面来说，真的很像一份真正的办公室工作。

93
00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.090
It really was.
确实如此。

94
00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.850
Just like hours at our desks.
就像在办公桌前呆了无数个小时。

95
00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.690
And the fluorescent light.
还有荧光灯。

96
00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:39.130
Yes.
没错。

97
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.030
I mean, that has a real effect on you.
我是说，那对人真的很有影响。

98
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:41.910
And the snacks.
还有零食。

99
00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:42.710
Come on.
拜托。

100
00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.230
That was the best spread.
那里的茶点真是太棒了。

101
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.150
Oh, God.
噢，天哪。

102
00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.090
We had the best, best food ever.
我们吃到了有史以来最棒、最美味的食物。

103
00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.830
It's all my dad ever talked about.
我爸以前聊的全是这个。

104
00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.310
All the years that he visited.
在他去过的那所有年里。

105
00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.770
And I would pepper him with questions about, so Steve Carell ate lunch with us today.
我会不停地追问他各种细节，比如史蒂夫·卡瑞尔今天跟我们一起吃了午饭。

106
00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.550
Wasn't that great?
不是很棒吗？

107
00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.030
And he was like, did you see the steak they had?
而他却说，你看到他们准备的牛排了吗？

108
00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.550
It was always about the food.
话题总是离不开吃的。

109
00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:01.490
Bill Kinsey.
比尔·金西。

110
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:02.770
Oh, Kate.
哦，凯特。

111
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.570
It's so good to see you.
很高兴见到你。

112
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.070
And Jenna.
还有珍娜。

113
00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.050
You guys.
你们几个。

114
00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:07.950
You guys.
你们大家。

115
00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:13.470
Kate, we always like to start by asking people how they came to be on The Office.
凯特，我们通常喜欢先问问大家是怎么加入《办公室》这部剧的。

116
00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.530
I actually auditioned for the pilot for the part of Jan.
我其实为试播集试镜过简这个角色。

117
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.690
Alison Jones said, I think you're really right for this show, but I don't know if this is
艾莉森·琼斯说，我觉得你真的很适合这部剧，但我不知道这算不算

118
00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.010
your part.
是你的角色。

119
00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.170
So clearly they went a different way with Melora Harden.
所以很显然，他们最终选了梅洛拉·哈登，走了不同的路线。

120
00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.110
And lo and behold, you guys shot the pilot.
结果呢，你们拍了试播集。

121
00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:31.930
I remember that summer, I was doing a sketch show once a week that was timed.
我记得那个夏天，我每周要做一次有时间限制的小品秀。

122
00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.110
It was a two-minute sketch show.
这是一个两分钟的小品秀。

123
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.130
So literally at two minutes, the lights would go out.
所以到了整整两分钟，灯光就会熄灭。

124
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:41.570
It was this live show in Hollywood at this theater on Melrose with one of the Scholar
这是在好莱坞梅尔罗斯剧院的一场现场演出，斯库勒

125
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.190
Brothers, Randy, was doing a sketch right before me.
兄弟中的兰迪就在我之前表演了一个小品。

126
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.650
He's like, have you been watching that British show, The Office?
他说，你有看那部英国剧集《办公室》吗？

127
00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:47.630
I'm so obsessed with it.
我简直迷死它了。

128
00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:49.290
He was like the first person to really tell me about it.
他是第一个真正向我提起这部剧的人。

129
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.350
I was like, yeah, I've seen a little bit.
我说，对啊，我看了一点点。

130
00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.810
He goes, you got to watch the whole thing.
他说，你得把整部剧都看完。

131
00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.890
So I kind of got obsessed.
于是我也有点着迷了。

132
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.750
And then come September, late August, early September, I had an audition.
然后到了九月份，八月下旬、九月初，我有个试镜。

133
00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:00.570
I couldn't make the first one because I was in Chicago with my aunt.
我错过了第一次试镜，因为我和我姑妈在芝加哥。

134
00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:01.610
And then I just came.
然后我就赶过来了。

135
00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.030
I figured the part was going to get taken.
我想象着这个角色肯定要被人拿下了。

136
00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:07.330
And they had another session a few days later.
结果他们在几天后又安排了一场试镜。

137
00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.790
And I went in and I read.
然后我去了，进行了试读。

138
00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.210
And I remember Alison Jones said, no makeup.
我记得艾莉森·琼斯说，不要化装。

139
00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:16.670
And usually in LA, you know, that means mascara, some foundation.
通常在洛杉矶，你知道的，那意味着刷点睫毛膏、打点粉底。

140
00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.890
It means something.
总得有点东西。

141
00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.230
It never really means no makeup, right?
其实从来不意味着真的不化妆，对吧？

142
00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.550
And they were like, literally, she literally had a box of tissues.
他们当时说，真的，她手里直接拿了一盒面巾纸。

143
00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.150
She's like, no makeup.
她说，不准化妆。

144
00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.590
Wipe it off.
擦掉。

145
00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:28.850
Get off, right?
卸掉，对吧？

146
00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:33.510
Anyway, and then I just remember there were a few actresses that I knew from Chicago that
不管怎样，然后我只记得现场有几个我从芝加哥认识的女演员

147
00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:33.810
were there.
也在那儿。

148
00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.150
And I felt like they booked everything.
我觉得她们把所有角色都拿下了。

149
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.430
I'm like, I'm never going to get this.
我想，我绝对拿不到这个角色了。

150
00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:41.770
But I just remember that room was Ken Quapas and Greg and Alison Jones.
但我只记得那个房间里有肯·夸帕斯、格雷格和艾莉森·琼斯。

151
00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.310
And I'm sure Paul Lieberstein.
而且我确信保罗·利伯斯坦也在。

152
00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.650
I'm sure there were, you know, Mike Scher.
我确信还有，你知道的，迈克·舒尔。

153
00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.750
I'm sure all the producers were there, the writer producers.
我确信所有的制片人都在，那些编剧兼制片人。

154
00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.410
It was like the most unique experience I think I'd ever had in an audition.
这绝对是我经历过的最独特的试镜体验。

155
00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.350
And then when I came out, I got home.
然后当我走出来时，我回到了家。

156
00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.230
And then Alison told me to go to Gower and do it again.
接着艾莉森叫我去高尔街再试一次。

157
00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.130
Do it one more time and do less, less, less, do less.
再试一次，要求是再少一点、再少一点、再少一点，少演一点。

158
00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.510
And then by the time I got home from there, I found out that I got the part.
然后等我从那儿回到家时，我发现我得到这个角色了。

159
00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:06.730
What?
什么？

160
00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.390
You booked it on the drive home.
你在开车回家的路上就拿下它了。

161
00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:08.710
Isn't that weird?
这不是很神奇吗？

162
00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:09.590
Girl, way to go.
天哪，干得好。

163
00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.590
And I didn't have a cell phone, so I didn't know till I got home.
而且我当时没有手机，所以直到到家才知道。

164
00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:12.750
That's every actor's dream.
那是每个演员的梦想。

