00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:49.910
That was so awesome.
那真是太棒了。

472
00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:53.110
Well, Kate, you're just, like, a rock star.
凯特，你简直就像个摇滚巨星。

473
00:18:53.110 --> 00:19:00.850
I mean, I have to ask you, though, if you were rolling with force into a windshield over and over and rolling off, were you sore?
不过我想问你，如果你一次又一次充满冲击力地滚向挡风玻璃又滚下来，你会觉得酸痛吗？

474
00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.270
Did you, like...
你会不会……

475
00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:08.330
We had to match what we shot before because they weren't sure about the before, if they were going to see us before.
我们必须和之前拍的镜头保持一致，因为他们之前不确定是否会拍到我们之前的画面。

476
00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.930
So I had to match the clothes.
所以我必须服装保持一致。

477
00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.830
And I was wearing short sleeves and, like, a denim jumper.
当时我穿着短袖，还有一条牛仔背心裙。

478
00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:14.990
Yeah.
对。

479
00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.070
Like a kindergarten teacher.
就像个幼儿园老师。

480
00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.730
And I remember the Emmys were, like, the next week.
我记得艾美奖就在第二周举行。

481
00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:20.010
And I was so bruised.
我身上青一块紫一块的。

482
00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.130
I had to use, like, body makeup.
我不得不使用身体粉底液之类的东西。

483
00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:27.930
Yeah, because I think if they knew they were going to do the stunt that way, they probably would have padded you up and dressed you accordingly, right?
对，因为我想如果他们早知道要那样拍特技，他们可能会给你做好防护，并给你做相应的服装搭配吧？

484
00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:28.270
Yes, totally, yeah.
是的，完全是这样，对。

485
00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:28.930
Yeah.
是的。

486
00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.030
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

487
00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:30.770
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

488
00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:33.630
Well, Kate, you did so many stunts on the show.
凯特，你在剧中做过好多特技动作。

489
00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.410
Was this your favorite?
这是你最喜欢的吗？

490
00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:36.310
Do you even have a favorite?
你甚至有最喜欢的吗？

491
00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:36.360
I think so.
我想是的。

492
00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.030
This was my favorite.
这是我最喜欢的。

493
00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.830
I also loved being on...
我也很喜欢在……

494
00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:39.610
This is so weird.
这太诡异了。

495
00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:43.710
I was on top of the men's room stall when Dwight comes...
当时德怀特来的时候，我正趴在男厕所的隔间顶部……

496
00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:44.690
I was planking.
我在玩平板支撑。

497
00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:45.910
Meredith is planking.
梅雷迪思在玩平板支撑。

498
00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:46.350
Yes, yes.
对，对。

499
00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:52.130
Dwight comes in with a fire extinguisher and just blows her off into the stall.
德怀特拿着灭火器冲进来，直接把她喷进了隔间里。

500
00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:53.370
Yeah.
对。

501
00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:59.450
We used the real men's room video village where the guests were, those two bathrooMs.
我们在客人所在的那个真正的男卫生间录像村拍的，就是那两间浴室。

502
00:19:59.690 --> 00:19:59.930
Yes, yeah.
对，没错。

503
00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:00.490
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

504
00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:05.070
And they put, like, this weird flim-flam mattress on top.
然后他们还在上面放了个奇怪的骗人薄床垫。

505
00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:09.850
And I was like, fingers crossed I don't go the other way because there was nothing on the other side.
当时我就想，千万别翻过去，因为另一边什么都没有，只能祈祷了。

506
00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.250
Because I had to balance.
因为我得保持平衡。

507
00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:12.750
It was so crazy.
太疯狂了。

508
00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.950
But, yeah, and it was really the men's room.
不过，对，那真的就是男卫生间。

509
00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:18.970
I'm like, okay, hopefully I don't land too hard because then I'm going to hit the toilet.
我就想，好吧，希望我落地别太重，不然就要撞到马桶了。

510
00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.130
It's so bizarre.
太离谱了。

511
00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:21.010
But it was really fun.
但真的很有趣。

512
00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:24.050
I want to give some props to your athleticism.
我想夸夸你的运动神经。

513
00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:29.850
I know that Angela has often chided me for my athleticism.
我知道安吉拉经常拿我的运动能力开涮。

514
00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:30.910
Here we go.
来了。

515
00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.250
No, no, it's okay.
不，不，没关系。

516
00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.790
I'm not going back to that anymore than I just did.
我不会再提这事了，就刚才那一下。

517
00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:40.650
But, Kate, you are amazingly athletic.
不过，凯特，你真的超级有运动天赋。

518
00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:43.370
I mean, in doing all these stunts, it doesn't surprise me.
我是说，拍所有这些特技时，我一点也不觉得意外。

519
00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.950
I mean, we know that you were on Dancing with the Stars and you were amazing.
我的意思是，我们知道你参加过《与星共舞》，而且表现惊艳。

520
00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:51.290
But you also did your lounge show, The Lampshades, for years and years and years.
但你还演了多年之久的休息室秀《灯罩》。

521
00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.390
And I remember coming to see you in that.
我记得我还去看过你的演出。

522
00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:57.790
And you do this deep squat.
而且你要做这种深蹲。

523
00:20:59.390 --> 00:20:59.790
Repeatedly.
反复地做。

524
00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:00.990
Repeatedly.
一遍又一遍。

525
00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.030
And you kick your leg up.
还要把腿高高踢起。

526
00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:05.970
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
当时我就想，天哪。

527
00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:12.870
I feel like they got so lucky with you as Meredith because you were qualified for these stunts.
我觉得剧组选你来演梅雷迪思真是太幸运了，因为你完全能应付这些特技。

528
00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:13.470
That's so sweet.
你太贴心了。

529
00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:15.770
I feel like for me, too, it was empowering.
我也觉得对我来说，这挺振奋人心的。

530
00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:18.610
Like, I did not do the stunt with my hair on fire.
比如，头发着火那个特技我没做。

531
00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.470
I did do all the stuff in the parking lot of Moroccan Christmas.
我在《摩洛哥圣诞节》停车场里的戏份全都是自己演的。

532
00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:22.990
I just didn't do the hair on fire.
我只是没做头发着火的那场。

533
00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.010
You did the bat.
你拿着球棒的那场。

534
00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.050
That was crazy.
那太疯狂了。

535
00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.310
And you really sold it.
而且你演得太入戏了。

536
00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:27.110
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

537
00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.610
And then I didn't actually shave my head.
然后我其实也没有剃光头。

538
00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:29.830
But I had a bald cap for that.
但我为此戴了个光头套。

539
00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:30.930
So I feel like those are the two.
所以我觉得这就是那两个特技。

540
00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:31.830
I'm like, OK.
我就想，好吧。

541
00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:35.170
But I think it's OK that you let your hair be.
但我觉得你保留头发也没关系。

542
00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.210
You know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

543
00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:36.530
I know.
我懂。

544
00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:38.190
I think Greg was disappointed, though.
不过我想格雷格当时挺失望的。

545
00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.290
It was like the first time I was like, nope, not doing that.
那好像是我第一次说，不，我不干。

546
00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.550
Well, can we talk a little bit about the moment in this episode where we're all in the hospital?
那我们能聊聊这集里大家都在医院里的那个场景吗？

547
00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:49.110
We've all come to see you.
我们都来看你了。

548
00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:53.690
My memory of this was it was so hard to get through those scenes without laughing.
我的记忆是，拍那些戏时要忍住不笑简直太难了。

549
00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.550
In fact, you see us break.
事实上，你能看到我们笑场了。

550
00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:55.850
Totally.
完全是。

551
00:21:55.850 --> 00:21:57.590
I fully break in the episode.
我完全插入了这一集。

552
00:21:57.590 --> 00:21:58.870
That was during Fun Run.
那是拍《欢乐跑》的时候。

553
00:21:58.990 --> 00:21:59.110
Yeah.
对。

554
00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.850
What are your memories of shooting in the hospital?
你对在医院拍摄有什么记忆？

555
00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:08.690
I remember there was one scene where Dwight talks about the fact that if they pulled the plug, you know, basically the energy.
我记得有一场戏，德怀特谈到如果他们拔掉插头，你知道的，基本上就是能量问题。

556
00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:11.430
Like they were wasting money keeping you going.
就像他们浪费钱维持你的生命一样。

557
00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:15.190
I loved it when you were like, do not pull the plug.
我特别喜欢你当时说，千万别拔插头。

558
00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:18.290
Don't pull any plugs.
什么插头都别拔。

559
00:22:18.430 --> 00:22:19.010
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

560
00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:19.530
It's so good.
太棒了。

561
00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:22.330
And I remember the take when Steve just has an apology.
而且我记得史蒂夫只想道歉的那条拍摄。

562
00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:23.510
He's trying to get an apology out of me.
他想让我向他道歉。

563
00:22:23.510 --> 00:22:24.290
And I won't apologize.
但我就是不道歉。

564
00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:24.990
I won't apologize.
我绝不道歉。

565
00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:28.070
And so he just decides to climb into the bed with me.
所以他干脆决定爬上我的病床。

566
00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:30.630
And I feel like I had a slight delayed reaction.
我觉得我的反应有点慢半拍。

567
00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:34.250
But I'm like, I just started screaming because I'm like, like.
但我开始尖叫，因为我觉得，就像是。

568
00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:38.670
Well, we were also surprised because he improvised that.
嗯，我们也吓了一跳，因为那是他即兴发挥的。

569
00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:40.230
And you even see all of us.
你甚至能看到我们所有人。

570
00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.310
We sort of like freeze.
我们有点像是直接僵住了。

571
00:22:41.550 --> 00:22:42.810
And then we're like, Michael, stop.
然后我们说，迈克尔，住手。

572
00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:43.350
Yes.
是的。

573
00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:44.150
Yes.
对。

574
00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:47.450
It really took us by surprise.
这真的让我们措手不及。

575
00:22:47.690 --> 00:22:47.990
Totally.
确实。

576
00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:48.730
Totally.
完全是。

577
00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:56.690
Well, Kate, another question we like to ask our guests is if they took anything with them when the show wrapped.
凯特，我们喜欢问嘉宾的另一个问题是，剧集杀青时他们有没有带走什么东西。

578
00:22:57.430 --> 00:22:58.650
How dare you?
你怎么敢这么问？

579
00:22:58.930 --> 00:22:59.190
I am not a thief.
我可不是小偷。

580
00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:00.210
Oh, what do you have it?
哦，你把它藏哪儿了？

581
00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:01.230
What do you have it for?
你留着它干嘛？

582
00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:07.070
Well, first of all, I have Meredith's purse, which I always wore it like a, you know, like a cross.
首先，我有梅雷迪思的钱包，我总是把它背得像个，你知道的，像个斜挎包。

583
00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:07.410
Like a side saddle.
就像侧跨那样。

584
00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:08.070
Yeah.
对。

585
00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:08.870
Yeah.
对。

586
00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:10.390
You satcheled it.
你把它当挎包背了。

587
00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:12.990
And I left everything in it that was still in there.
里面原本的东西我都原封不动地留着。

588
00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:19.990
So this is why I still had the marriage union of Pamela Morgan Beasley and James Duncan Halpert.
所以这就是为什么我还留着帕梅拉·摩根·比斯利和詹姆斯·邓肯·哈尔珀特的结婚证书。

589
00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:21.810
Is that our wedding?
那是我们的婚礼吗？

590
00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:22.270
Yes.
是的。

591
00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:23.030
It's the program.
这是流程单。

592
00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:24.050
So this is what I did.
所以我当时是这么做的。

593
00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:24.770
It's our wedding program.
这是我们的婚礼流程单。

594
00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:25.430
The wedding party.
伴郎伴娘团。

595
00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.190
And the wedding party.
还有伴郎伴娘团。

596
00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:26.490
Yes.
对。

597
00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:32.450
This is what I showed on Some Good News with John Krasinski when we did our wedding dance.
这就是我和约翰·卡拉辛斯基办婚礼舞会时，我在《一些好消息》节目里展示的东西。

598
00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:33.230
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

599
00:23:33.310 --> 00:23:33.930
Isn't that crazy?
这不是很疯狂吗？

600
00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:37.890
That is so – that you had just tucked it in your purse and you still have it.
太疯狂了——你竟然把它塞在钱包里，而且到现在还留着。

601
00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:38.150
I did.
我做过。

602
00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.350
We would do that, though.
不过我们以前确实会那样。

603
00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:40.810
We would get prop purses.
我们会准备道具包包。

604
00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:43.810
And, like, if we had props, we would just put them in our purse.
而且，如果有道具的话，我们就会直接把它们放进包里。

605
00:23:43.930 --> 00:23:44.070
Totally.
完全是。

606
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:44.490
Yeah.
对。

607
00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:45.730
I have – oh, my gosh.
我有——哦，天哪。

608
00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:46.450
What else do I have in here?
我这里面还有什么？

609
00:23:46.590 --> 00:23:47.890
I think I have –
我想我有——

610
00:23:47.890 --> 00:23:49.030
Do you have some old sides?
你有一些旧剧本页吗？

611
00:23:49.150 --> 00:23:50.750
I would always put my sides in my purse.
我以前总是把剧本页放进包里。

612
00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:50.850
Yes, I do have sides.
没错，我确实有剧本页。

613
00:23:50.850 --> 00:23:54.970
But I also have – I have Sweeney Todd from when Andy was performing in that theater.
但我也有一份——安迪在那家剧院演出时的《理发师陶德》。

614
00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:55.550
Wow.
哇。

615
00:23:55.770 --> 00:24:03.170
And I have Church of Angels, Cecilia Marie Halpert when she got christened.
还有《天使教堂》，塞西莉亚·玛丽·哈尔珀特受洗时的。

616
00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:04.130
Cece's christened.
西西受洗了。

617
00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:05.850
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

618
00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:06.050
Wow.
哇。

619
00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:07.530
Kate, these are amazing.
凯特，这些太棒了。

620
00:24:07.690 --> 00:24:08.090
I know.
我知道。

621
00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:10.310
Well, Kate, fans love Meredith.
话说，凯特，粉丝们很喜欢梅雷迪斯。

622
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.210
And you know we're going to be hitting you up.
而且你知道我们要联系你了。

623
00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:16.710
We've got a few more episodes to cover before we're done here.
在我们结束这里的工作之前，我们还有几集要聊。

624
00:24:17.090 --> 00:24:20.510
Before we say goodbye, is there anything we can share with everyone?
在我们说再见之前，有什么可以和大家分享的吗？

625
00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:21.670
Like, where to find you?
比如，在哪里能找到你？

626
00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:22.530
What you're up to?
你最近在忙什么？

627
00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:23.810
Yes.
有的。

628
00:24:24.450 --> 00:24:28.010
I – well, on Instagram, at TheRealKateFlannery.
我——嗯，在Instagram上，是TheRealKateFlannery。

629
00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:29.890
On Twitter, at KateFlannery.
在Twitter上，是KateFlannery。

630
00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:33.190
I go to a little ramen place once a week in K-10.
我每周去K-10的一家小拉面馆一次。

631
00:24:33.470 --> 00:24:33.790
Don't say that.
别说这个。

632
00:24:35.130 --> 00:24:41.350
But I'm actually doing some charity work for Phil Abundance, which is the biggest food bank
但我实际上在为“丰盛费城”做一些慈善工作，那是费城最大的食品银行。

633
00:24:41.350 --> 00:24:41.930
in Philadelphia.
在费城。

634
00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:43.110
That's my hometown.
