1110
00:46:30.140 --> 00:46:32.980
Can you imagine if some of the writers had had their way?
你能想象如果有些编剧如愿以偿会怎么样吗？

1111
00:46:33.620 --> 00:46:34.520
I know.
我知道。

1112
00:46:34.880 --> 00:46:35.600
No kidding.
可不是嘛。

1113
00:46:36.020 --> 00:46:36.500
Gosh.
天哪。

1114
00:46:37.960 --> 00:46:40.220
Well, now Pam is going to go around the office.
好了，现在帕姆要在办公室里走动了。

1115
00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:42.600
She thinks everyone should visit Meredith.
她觉得每个人都应该去探望梅雷迪思。

1116
00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:45.420
And she's collecting money so they can buy her flowers.
她还在收钱，好给梅雷迪思买花。

1117
00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:46.880
Yes.
对。

1118
00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:50.260
But Angela says she can't go because Sprinkles is sick.
但安吉拉说她不能去，因为斯普林克斯生病了。

1119
00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:50.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1120
00:46:50.920 --> 00:46:56.380
And Angela needs to go home at lunch to give Sprinkles some medicine and eat lunch with her cat.
安吉拉需要在午休时回家给斯普林克斯喂药，并和她的猫一起吃午饭。

1121
00:46:56.580 --> 00:46:56.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1122
00:46:56.880 --> 00:47:02.340
And you guys, there are wonderful deleted talking heads from this episode.
各位，这集里还有精彩的被删减单采呢。

1123
00:47:02.720 --> 00:47:04.520
So many characters have great talking heads.
很多角色都有很棒的单采镜头。

1124
00:47:04.680 --> 00:47:10.080
But this is a talking head that would have happened right before Pam walked over to Angela.
但这本来是一个在帕姆走向安吉拉之前就会出现的单采。

1125
00:47:10.300 --> 00:47:12.060
And I have to read it to you because it's so fun to me.
我得读给你们听，因为我觉得太有趣了。

1126
00:47:12.740 --> 00:47:14.340
Angela has a talking head that says,
安吉拉有一个单采镜头说：

1127
00:47:14.340 --> 00:47:16.780
I've had Sprinkles for 16 years.
我养斯普林克斯16年了。

1128
00:47:17.040 --> 00:47:19.920
I adopted her when I graduated from accounting school.
我从会计学校毕业时收养了她。

1129
00:47:20.320 --> 00:47:22.300
I knew the kind of life I wanted.
我知道我想要什么样的生活。

1130
00:47:22.680 --> 00:47:27.820
One with the companionship and unpredictable good times only a cat offers.
那种只有猫才能提供的陪伴和意想不到的美好时光的生活。

1131
00:47:28.960 --> 00:47:29.740
Hmm.
嗯。

1132
00:47:30.980 --> 00:47:34.460
The unpredictable good times a cat offers.
猫所提供的意想不到的美好时光。

1133
00:47:35.140 --> 00:47:38.840
You know, cats really do offer unpredictable good times.
你知道，猫确实能带来意想不到的美好时光。

1134
00:47:39.480 --> 00:47:42.980
Creed Bratton has texted me this sentence.
克里德·布拉顿给我发过这句话。

1135
00:47:42.980 --> 00:47:46.700
It's an unpredictable good time only a cat offers.
那是只有猫才能提供的意想不到的美好时光。

1136
00:47:47.300 --> 00:47:48.960
Creed texted me that the other day.
克里德前几天给我发了这条。

1137
00:47:49.860 --> 00:47:50.860
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1138
00:47:51.200 --> 00:47:52.000
So, yes.
所以，是的。

1139
00:47:52.260 --> 00:47:55.740
So, Angela has that talking head that you didn't get to see.
所以，安吉拉有那个你们没能看到的单采。

1140
00:47:55.740 --> 00:47:59.240
And it really sort of builds up, like, this is, like, more than a cat to her.
这真的有点像是在铺垫，对她来说，这不仅仅是一只猫。

1141
00:47:59.340 --> 00:48:00.680
I mean, we already know that.
我的意思是，我们早就知道了。

1142
00:48:00.820 --> 00:48:08.220
But when Pam suggests that Angela, like, should go and that she's, like,
但当帕姆建议安吉拉去探望，并且觉得她好像是在……

1143
00:48:08.460 --> 00:48:12.580
ditching on her party planning committee duties, Angela's ticked.
逃避派对策划委员会的职责时，安吉拉气坏了。

1144
00:48:12.980 --> 00:48:14.720
Uh, Sam, can I get a Pam Sass?
呃，萨姆，能来点帕姆式的犀利吗？

1145
00:48:15.540 --> 00:48:16.660
Pam Sass!
帕姆式犀利！

1146
00:48:16.860 --> 00:48:17.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:48:18.240 --> 00:48:19.780
We had some people write in.
我们有一些人写信来了。

1148
00:48:19.900 --> 00:48:20.780
Paige Banker.
佩姬·班克尔。

1149
00:48:21.080 --> 00:48:22.280
Lauren Corwin.
劳伦·科温。

1150
00:48:22.960 --> 00:48:24.760
They just wrote in all caps,
她们全用大写字母写道：

1151
00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:28.660
MAJOR PAM SASS at 5 minutes 35 seconds.
帕姆·萨斯少校在5分35秒处。

1152
00:48:28.940 --> 00:48:29.360
Yeah.
对。

1153
00:48:29.360 --> 00:48:30.820
I agree, you guys.
我同意，伙计们。

1154
00:48:31.580 --> 00:48:32.540
Pam says,
帕姆说：

1155
00:48:32.920 --> 00:48:34.760
Can't your other cats keep her company?
你的其他猫不能陪陪她吗？

1156
00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:36.320
And Angela's like,
然后安吉拉说：

1157
00:48:36.500 --> 00:48:37.740
There's bad blood.
有宿怨。

1158
00:48:38.160 --> 00:48:38.720
Jealousies.
有嫉妒。

1159
00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:39.520
Clicks.
有小团体。

1160
00:48:39.740 --> 00:48:41.860
What's happening at this woman's house?
这个女人的家里到底在发生什么？

1161
00:48:45.500 --> 00:48:49.220
Um, I have to tell you something about this scene.
嗯，关于这个场景，我得跟你说件事。

1162
00:48:50.680 --> 00:48:57.360
This was what I thought you were going to tell me when you said that I had written you an email about this episode.
这就是你之前说我给你发过关于这集的邮件时，我以为你要跟我说的事。

1163
00:48:57.540 --> 00:48:57.800
Why?
为什么？

1164
00:48:57.800 --> 00:48:59.820
And about what I was doing this week.
以及关于我这周在做的事。

1165
00:49:00.040 --> 00:49:00.240
Why?
为什么？

1166
00:49:01.420 --> 00:49:07.360
Lady, I was really, really hungover when we shot this scene.
天哪，拍这场戏的时候我真的宿醉得厉害。

1167
00:49:07.740 --> 00:49:09.780
Like, super hungover.
真的，超级宿醉。

1168
00:49:09.960 --> 00:49:18.600
And if you look at me in this scene compared to every other scene, you can see it on my face.
如果你把这场戏里的我和其他所有戏里的我作对比，你就能从我脸上看出来。

1169
00:49:18.600 --> 00:49:20.940
I am like, I am gray.
我简直，我脸色发灰。

1170
00:49:21.320 --> 00:49:23.040
I'm kind of green.
我甚至有点发绿。

1171
00:49:23.420 --> 00:49:23.860
Why?
为什么？

1172
00:49:23.860 --> 00:49:25.860
My eyes are puffy.
我的眼睛肿了。

1173
00:49:25.860 --> 00:49:27.580
I will never forget it.
我永远不会忘记。

1174
00:49:28.140 --> 00:49:37.780
So, the night before this shoot, I went to a Mexican restaurant, and I was with a friend who ordered a margarita.
所以，拍摄的前一晚，我去了一家墨西哥餐厅，和一个点了一杯玛格丽特酒的朋友在一起。

1175
00:49:38.040 --> 00:49:38.360
Okay.
好吧。

1176
00:49:39.220 --> 00:49:42.100
I had never really had a margarita before.
我以前其实没怎么喝过玛格丽特酒。

1177
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:43.680
Oh, no way.
哦，不会吧。

1178
00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:46.280
Yes, yes, it's true.
真的，真的，千真万确。

1179
00:49:46.520 --> 00:49:48.180
I, we've talked about this.
我，我们讨论过这个。

1180
00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:51.820
I did not have a lot of experience with drinking.
我没有什么饮酒经验。

1181
00:49:51.820 --> 00:49:55.020
I just, you know, I had a cosmopolitan.
我只是，你知道的，我喝过大都会鸡尾酒。

1182
00:49:55.220 --> 00:49:58.100
I had to research drinking in order to play Drunk Pam.
为了演好醉酒的帕姆，我还特意去研究了喝酒。

1183
00:49:58.280 --> 00:49:59.860
So, I took a sip of it.
所以，我抿了一口。

1184
00:49:59.920 --> 00:50:00.200
Yeah.
对。

1185
00:50:00.380 --> 00:50:03.820
And I was like, this is delicious.
当时我就想，这也太好喝了吧。

1186
00:50:05.200 --> 00:50:06.800
I love this drink.
我太喜欢这杯酒了。

1187
00:50:07.100 --> 00:50:07.800
Uh-oh.
噢哦。

1188
00:50:07.900 --> 00:50:09.200
And then I had three.
然后我喝了三杯。

1189
00:50:09.440 --> 00:50:09.960
Three?
三杯？

1190
00:50:10.960 --> 00:50:12.980
Three over the course of this dinner.
在这顿饭的过程中喝了三杯。

1191
00:50:13.700 --> 00:50:13.960
Yeah.
对。

1192
00:50:13.960 --> 00:50:22.550
I, then, you know, lady, this scene was the first scene of the next day.
我，然后，你知道的，天哪，这场戏是第二天最早的一场。

1193
00:50:22.730 --> 00:50:27.550
We had a super early call time, and I was really feeling it.
我们的通告时间超级早，我真的是深有体会。

1194
00:50:27.730 --> 00:50:33.110
Like, I didn't, I had not had enough time to recover from my three margaritas.
就是，我，我根本没有足够的时间从那三杯玛格丽特酒里缓过来。

1195
00:50:33.370 --> 00:50:33.890
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1196
00:50:34.070 --> 00:50:37.170
My call times were routinely, like, 5 a.m., 5.30.
我平时的通告时间通常就是早上5点、5点半这样。

1197
00:50:37.170 --> 00:50:40.710
So, you were, you were sweating tequila.
所以，你当时，你当时浑身都在冒龙舌兰酒的汗。

1198
00:50:41.710 --> 00:50:42.270
I was.
是的。

1199
00:50:42.390 --> 00:50:47.030
And so, I thought when you said earlier that you had an email from me about what I was doing
所以，刚才你跟我说你收到过我关于我这周在做什么的邮件时，

1200
00:50:47.030 --> 00:50:52.310
this week, I was like, oh, my gosh, did I write Angela about those margaritas?
我还以为，天哪，我是不是写信跟安吉拉坦白那些玛格丽特酒的事了？

1201
00:50:53.450 --> 00:50:54.590
Sorry to disappoint.
抱歉让你失望了。

1202
00:50:54.590 --> 00:50:59.290
You had a mandatory physical table read and a sexual harassment seminar.
你们有一场强制性的全员剧本围读会和一次性骚扰研讨会。

1203
00:51:00.350 --> 00:51:00.830
Exactly.
没错。

1204
00:51:00.830 --> 00:51:03.890
Anyway, that's my little, that's my little tidbit.
总之，这就是我的小花絮。

1205
00:51:04.110 --> 00:51:10.410
Every time I see this scene, I'm reminded of the night that I first drank three margaritas.
每次我看到这个场景，就会想起我第一次喝三杯玛格丽塔的那个晚上。

1206
00:51:10.650 --> 00:51:12.330
Well, now I'll always remember it.
好吧，现在我也会永远记住它了。

1207
00:51:12.550 --> 00:51:17.750
So, now Michael has to call Ryan, because Ryan is his boss, and tell him he hit Meredith
所以，现在迈克尔必须给瑞安打电话，因为瑞安是他的老板，告诉他他撞了梅雷迪思

1208
00:51:17.750 --> 00:51:19.670
on company property.
在公司资产上。

1209
00:51:20.290 --> 00:51:21.890
With his company car.
用他的公司车。

1210
00:51:22.010 --> 00:51:22.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1211
00:51:23.170 --> 00:51:25.890
And Ryan is such a badass boss in this.
而且瑞安在这段里真是个硬汉老板。

1212
00:51:26.010 --> 00:51:30.410
He's clearly, he's liking being the boss and talking to Michael this way.
他显然很享受当老板的感觉，也喜欢这样跟迈克尔说话。

1213
00:51:31.070 --> 00:51:37.330
Well, and then we go to the Ryan talking head, and Ryan has a new look.
嗯，然后镜头转到瑞安的采访画面，瑞安换了个新造型。

1214
00:51:37.450 --> 00:51:37.690
Oh.
哦。

1215
00:51:37.890 --> 00:51:41.630
He's got his, like, his, what do you call that?
他留着那种，怎么说呢？

1216
00:51:41.630 --> 00:51:42.650
It's not a beard.
这不是胡子。

1217
00:51:42.690 --> 00:51:44.870
It's like a, the permanent stubble.
这就像是，那种永远刮不干净的胡渣。

1218
00:51:44.910 --> 00:51:47.530
Yeah, it's like a 5 o'clock shadow, but it's a choice.
对，就像傍晚刚长出来的胡渣，但这是故意留的。

1219
00:51:47.710 --> 00:51:48.550
It's a choice.
是故意为之的。

1220
00:51:48.830 --> 00:51:49.150
Yeah.
对。

1221
00:51:49.450 --> 00:51:51.650
Yeah, and his hair's all slicked back.
对，而且他的头发全都往后梳了。

1222
00:51:52.090 --> 00:51:54.950
He's got, like, kind of a Gordon Gekko thing going on.
他有点像华尔街里的戈登·盖柯那种感觉。

1223
00:51:55.050 --> 00:51:57.430
Yeah, he looks like he should be in the show Succession.
对，他看起来就像应该去演《继承之战》一样。

1224
00:51:57.550 --> 00:51:58.590
That's what he looks like.
他看起来就是那样。

1225
00:51:59.010 --> 00:51:59.450
Yes.
是的。

1226
00:51:59.730 --> 00:51:59.990
Right?
对吧？

1227
00:51:59.990 --> 00:52:02.610
And he has the same kind of, like, cheesy attitude.
而且他有一种那种油腔滑调的态度。

1228
00:52:02.830 --> 00:52:05.810
He's like, some people keep calling me, you know, wonder kid.
他就像是，有些人总是在叫我，你知道的，神童。

1229
00:52:06.090 --> 00:52:07.750
You know, not really sure what that means.
你知道，其实不太确定那是什么意思。

1230
00:52:07.830 --> 00:52:09.130
Well, I guess I do know what it means.
好吧，我想我确实知道是什么意思。

1231
00:52:09.250 --> 00:52:10.730
He's, oh, it's so cringy.
他，噢，真是太尴尬了。

1232
00:52:11.090 --> 00:52:12.070
Yeah, it's great.
对，这太棒了。

1233
00:52:12.230 --> 00:52:16.690
This is, we're going to get a glimpse now of what this new dynamic is going to be like.
这就是，我们现在要一窥这种新的人际关系会是什么样了。

1234
00:52:17.310 --> 00:52:25.110
Well, then we have a scene that I love, Angela, because it's a Dwight and Angela secret scene.
好吧，接下来有一个我特别喜欢的场景，安吉拉，因为这是一场德怀特和安吉拉的秘密戏份。

1235
00:52:25.990 --> 00:52:29.110
Remember, the people in the office, we don't know you're dating, right?
记住，办公室里的人，我们还不知道你们在交往，对吧？

1236
00:52:29.270 --> 00:52:32.810
So you guys are still kind of like a secret couple.
所以你们俩其实还是那种秘密情侣。

1237
00:52:32.950 --> 00:52:38.030
Whenever you want to talk to each other, you have to go be, like, weirdly secretive about it.
每当你们想跟对方说话时，都得表现得神神秘秘、奇奇怪怪的。

1238
00:52:38.150 --> 00:52:38.490
Yeah.
对。

1239
00:52:38.490 --> 00:52:40.790
I mean, I guess only Jim knows, right?
我是说，我想只有吉姆知道，对吧？

1240
00:52:41.850 --> 00:52:42.650
And Pam.
还有帕姆。

1241
00:52:42.810 --> 00:52:43.210
And Pam.
还有帕姆。

1242
00:52:43.470 --> 00:52:46.210
Have Jim and Pam hopefully talked about it at this point?
吉姆和帕姆这时候希望已经谈过这事了吧？

1243
00:52:46.210 --> 00:52:47.330
We still don't know.
我们还是不知道。

1244
00:52:47.470 --> 00:52:48.130
You would think.
你本以为会的。

1245
00:52:48.530 --> 00:52:56.130
So, lady, I had a long speech where I talk about all of Sprinkles medications, and I did that thing like you did on beach games.
所以，女士，我有一段很长的台词，讲的是斯普林克尔的所有药物，我做了像你在《海滩游戏》里做的那样的事。

1246
00:52:56.270 --> 00:53:01.010
I learned it backwards and forwards so that I could say it just effortlessly, you know?
我把它正着背倒着背都学会了，这样我可以说得毫不费力，你知道吗？

1247
00:53:01.190 --> 00:53:02.330
But here it is.
但就是这样。

1248
00:53:02.430 --> 00:53:03.730
Sam, can you play that clip?
萨姆，你能播放一下那个片段吗？

1249
00:53:04.070 --> 00:53:05.130
So what do you need me to do?
所以你需要我做什么？

1250
00:53:05.310 --> 00:53:06.010
I wrote it out.
我都写下来了。

1251
00:53:06.210 --> 00:53:06.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1252
00:53:06.670 --> 00:53:07.770
There's a diabetes shot.
有一针糖尿病注射。

1253
00:53:07.990 --> 00:53:09.310
Roll the insulin in your hands.
把胰岛素在手里揉搓一下。

1254
00:53:09.490 --> 00:53:10.210
Don't shake it.
不要摇晃它。

1255
00:53:10.370 --> 00:53:12.130
She gets an ACE inhibitor with her meal.
她吃饭时要吃一剂血管紧张素转化酶抑制剂。

1256
00:53:12.350 --> 00:53:15.570
If you have to put her right in front of the dish or she won't see it because of the cataracts.
如果你必须把她直接放在盘子前面，否则她会因为白内障看不到。

1257
00:53:16.050 --> 00:53:19.690
Mix one capsule of omega fatty acid in with her kidney medicine.
将一粒欧米伽脂肪酸胶囊混入她的肾脏药物中。

1258
00:53:20.430 --> 00:53:23.630
And you want to give that to her 15 minutes after she's eaten.
你得在她吃完饭15分钟后喂她。

1259
00:53:24.450 --> 00:53:28.310
And, oh, there's a fungal cream because she has this infection under her tail.
哦，对了，还有一种真菌药膏，因为她尾巴下面有感染。

1260
00:53:28.430 --> 00:53:31.830
So you're going to have to lift her tail and put the cream right at the base of her tail.
所以你得抬起她的尾巴，把药膏抹在尾巴根部。

1261
00:53:32.550 --> 00:53:37.130
I love that you memorized it, Angela, because when I watched that, I wondered.
安吉拉，我很高兴你把它背下来了，因为我看的时候就在想。

